         "Whereas broiler chicks require 22–23% CP in the starter phase, **Turkey Poults (0–4 wk)** require **28% Crude Protein** (and 2800 kcal ME/kg; C:P ratio ~100:1) and **Japanese Quail Chicks (0–3 wk)** require **26–27% Crude Protein** (and 2800–2900 kcal ME/kg, dropping to 20% CP in laying quail). This high protein density is driven by their explosive early post-hatch lean tissue and feather growth rates.",
